var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"reference/developer_guidelines/#Developer-Guidelines","page":"Developer Guidelines","text":"In order to contribute to PowerSystemsUpdater.jl repository please read the following sections of InfrastructureSystems.jl documentation in detail:\n\nStyle Guide\nDocumentation Best Practices\nContributing Guidelines\n\nPull requests are always welcome to fix bugs or add additional modeling capabilities.\n\nAll the code contributions need to include tests with a minimum coverage of 70%","title":"Developer Guidelines"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/internal/#Internal-API","page":"Internals","text":"","title":"Internal API"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ATTRIBUTE_DERIVATIONS","page":"Internals","text":"Supplemental attribute fields mapped onto differently named PSY6 fields, by attribute type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ATTRIBUTE_DERIVATIONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.CONDITIONALLY_REQUIRED_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"VSC setpoints the schema requires only for the quantity the control mode selects, which their optional type does not show (VSC_SETPOINT_FIELDS).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.CONDITIONALLY_REQUIRED_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.CONTROL_OBJECTIVE_BANDS","page":"Internals","text":"The bands the schema requires on a TransformerCircuit for each control_objective.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.CONTROL_OBJECTIVE_BANDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.DATA_DISCRIMINATORS","page":"Internals","text":"Discriminators whose value is data in the record, not a basis the updater chooses.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.DATA_DISCRIMINATORS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.DC_VOLTAGE_NO_LIMIT","page":"Internals","text":"The \"no limit\" maximum of a VSC DC voltage band: 999.9 in PSY5 (per unit) and PSY6 (kV).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.DC_VOLTAGE_NO_LIMIT"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.DIRECT_TYPES","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 types that map onto an identically named PSY6 model by a plain field copy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.DIRECT_TYPES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.DYNAMIC_REFERENCE_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 fields linking a static device to its dynamic model. The schema has no dynamic models, so the link is dropped (and reported) and the static device kept.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.DYNAMIC_REFERENCE_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.MARKET_BID_COST_DEFAULTED_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY6 required fields with no PSY5 counterpart, mapped to the builder for the zero-cost value that stands in. Unlike MARKET_BID_COST_SCALAR_FIELDS this is not a promotion of PSY5 data — PSY5 either has no field here at all or writes an explicit null — so it only applies when the value is missing, never overwriting one PSY5 did supply.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.MARKET_BID_COST_DEFAULTED_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.MARKET_BID_COST_SCALAR_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 permits MarketBidCost.shut_down to be a bare scalar; PSY6 types it as a concrete InputOutputCurve. The schema sanctions this promotion: the field's description documents the \"legacy scalar promotion\", and its default gives exactly the InputOutputCurve/LinearFunctionData shape built here (Core/common.json). Promotes the scalar s into a constant function (proportional_term = 0.0, i.e. the multiplier, so the curve's value is just s) rather than dropping it — PSY5's use of 0.0 here is a real \"no extra cost\" curve, not a missing value. Built as a raw PSY5-shaped nested dict so the promoted curve goes through the ordinary ONEOF_DISCRIMINATORS injection on the recursive pass right after, instead of a second, hand-rolled discriminator mechanism.\n\nPSY5's no_load_cost is NOT included here: PSY6's counterpart field is minimum_energy_offer (a /MWh curve, not the same physical quantity), and the schema documents the conversion as minimum_energy_offer = no_load_cost / P_min — P_min lives on the owning generator, not on this cost object, so the division cannot be done from here. Promoting the bare scalar into a curve without that division would silently mislabel a /h value as /MWh. Left unmapped and recorded on the report instead of forced.\n\nminimum_energy_offer is separately defaulted below (MARKET_BID_COST_DEFAULTED_FIELDS) whenever PSY5 supplies no value at all: the field is required on the PSY6 struct, and Core/common.json documents this exact zero-cost shape as its schema default — the same default a codegen consumer without vendor extensions would fall back to.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.MARKET_BID_COST_SCALAR_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.MULTIPLIER_QUANTITY_KINDS","page":"Internals","text":"The physical quantity a normalized series scales back to, keyed by the PSY5 accessor that named the base.\n\nValues are quantity_types names from SiennaSchemas' Core/units.json, the vocabulary PSY6's quantity_kind column draws on. With unit_system set to COMPONENT_BASE the values are dimensionless, so this is the only remaining record of what they measure.\n\nThe reservoir accessors (get_storage_capacity, get_storage_target, get_inflow) are deliberately absent: their quantity depends on the owning reservoir's level_data_type (a level is an energy, a volume, or a head), which is not resolvable from an association row. _quantity_kind reports those rather than guessing one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.MULTIPLIER_QUANTITY_KINDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.NO_CURRENT_LIMIT_KA","page":"Internals","text":"The schema's \"no limit\" DC current in kA (PowerSystems' INFINITE_CURRENT).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.NO_CURRENT_LIMIT_KA"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ONEOF_DISCRIMINATORS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 type name -> (PSY6 discriminator property, discriminator value). PSY5 has no such field; the value comes from __metadata__.type, not a formula on the name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ONEOF_DISCRIMINATORS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PER_UNIT_PRONE_UNITS","page":"Internals","text":"Physical units PSY5 commonly stored per unit; an unknown-storage field in one is reported.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PER_UNIT_PRONE_UNITS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.POWER_UNITS","page":"Internals","text":"Power units, in which a per-unit value is a multiple of a base MVA.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.POWER_UNITS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSSE_CONTROL_CODE","page":"Internals","text":"PSS/E COD code of each PSY5 TransformerControlObjective.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSSE_CONTROL_CODE"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_DEFAULT_VOLTAGE_SETPOINT","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5's default TapTransformer.voltage_setpoint, filled in for older files that omit it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_DEFAULT_VOLTAGE_SETPOINT"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_DEVICE_BASE_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 fields stored per unit on the component's own base_power (the system base for a component with none): every field PSY5's descriptors mark needs_conversion, as (type, field) => conversion_unit. The unit names the physical quantity PSY5's getters convert it to (mva for power, ohm for impedance, ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_DEVICE_BASE_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_DURATION_PATTERNS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5's duration encoding, one pattern per Dates.Period its writer emitted.\n\nOrdered, and the first match wins, because the patterns overlap: P0DT3600.000S is a Millisecond while P0DT3600S is a Second, and P1M is a month while P0DT1M is a minute. This is the same ordered table the writer's own reader used.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_DURATION_PATTERNS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_FIELD_RENAMES","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 fields PSY6 spells differently: (PSY5 type, PSY5 field) => PSY6 field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_FIELD_RENAMES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_FUEL_UNITS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 FuelCurve has no fuel_units: its y axis is MMBTU per hour by PSY5 convention. PSY6 requires the field, so a FuelCurve without it gets \"MMBTU\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_FUEL_UNITS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_INTERNAL_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 keys that never become PSY6 properties on the entity. services becomes ServiceAssociation rows (_add_service_associations!) and ext goes to the document's ext table (_carry_ext!); internal and __metadata__ are serialization scaffolding.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_INTERNAL_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_NO_CURRENT_LIMITS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5's \"no limit\" DC currents (PSS/E IMAX of 0, and the constructor default).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_NO_CURRENT_LIMITS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_STORAGE","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 fields not stored as device-base per unit, which PSY5's descriptors do not record, by type and field name as it reaches build_kwargs (after translator renames). \"*\" matches any type. Comments cite the PSY5 convention.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_STORAGE"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_TS_METADATA_ROOT_PATH","page":"Internals","text":"The HDF5 dataset PSY5 embeds its metadata SQLite database in.\n\nNamed here rather than read from IS.HDF5_TS_METADATA_ROOT_PATH because that constant no longer exists: IS moved its storage to InfraStore and dropped HDF5 entirely. The path describes the legacy on-disk format this package reads, so it belongs to the reader.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_TS_METADATA_ROOT_PATH"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_TS_ROOT_PATH","page":"Internals","text":"The HDF5 group PSY5 keys its time series arrays under, one subgroup per time series UUID, each holding a data dataset plus module/type/data_type attributes.\n\nNamed here rather than imported because IS dropped HDF5 storage when it moved to InfraStore. The constant describes the legacy format this package reads, so it belongs to the reader.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PSY5_TS_ROOT_PATH"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.REGULATED_BUS_OBJECTIVES","page":"Internals","text":"Objectives under which a TransformerCircuit names the bus its tap regulates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.REGULATED_BUS_OBJECTIVES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.REPORT_SECTIONS","page":"Internals","text":"Report fields in display order, with each one's section title.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.REPORT_SECTIONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.RESERVED_FEATURE_NAMES","page":"Internals","text":"Feature names PSY6 reserves because they name a field of a time series or of the key that addresses one (the TimeSeriesFeatures.propertyNames exclusion in SiennaSchemas). PSY5 had no such rule, and tools that build PSY5 systems from other models write some of them (a model year as horizon), so _features renames them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.RESERVED_FEATURE_NAMES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.RESERVE_DIRECTIONS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 carries reserve direction as a type parameter (VariableReserve{ReserveUp}); PSY6 carries it as a field with a different vocabulary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.RESERVE_DIRECTIONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.SERIES_KEY_TYPES","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 key types, by the association time_series_types each can name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.SERIES_KEY_TYPES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.SERIES_REF_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 fields that may hold a time series key, by owner type, and the PSY6 field that replaces it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.SERIES_REF_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.SWITCHED_ADMITTANCE_LIMITS_FIELD","page":"Internals","text":"The PSY6 field admittance_limits (PSS/E VSWLO/VSWHI) lands in, by control mode. FIXED and UNDEFINED use neither, so their band is kept in ext.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.SWITCHED_ADMITTANCE_LIMITS_FIELD"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.TAP_MOVING_OBJECTIVES","page":"Internals","text":"Objectives that move the tap. The schema lets tap_ratio_limits default to 0.9-1.1, but PowerSystems 6 rejects such a circuit without them (branchdata_checks.jl), so they are always written.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.TAP_MOVING_OBJECTIVES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.THREE_WINDING_BASE_POWER_KEY","page":"Internals","text":"The pair base each winding's values are stored on (PSY5 _get_winding_base_power), used as the circuit's base_power so the values are not scaled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.THREE_WINDING_BASE_POWER_KEY"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.TIME_SERIES_POINTER_TYPES","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 sometimes embeds a time series key in a value field. Where PSY6 names the series by association id (SERIES_REF_FIELDS) the key is carried across as that id; anywhere else dropping it would silently lose data, so it is an error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.TIME_SERIES_POINTER_TYPES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.TYPES_WITHOUT_EXT","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 types whose PSY6 model has no ext; PowerSystems' importer ignores their entries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.TYPES_WITHOUT_EXT"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.UNIT_BASES","page":"Internals","text":"Values a unit discriminator can take, in order of preference.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.UNIT_BASES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.UNMAPPED_EXT_KEY","page":"Internals","text":"The ext key holding a component's PSY5 values with no PSY6 field, as field => value (a nested struct's field is Type.field), as PSY5 stored them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.UNMAPPED_EXT_KEY"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.VARIABLE_OPERATION_COST_TYPES","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 spells the variable cost field variable on these four cost types; PSY6 spells it variable_operation_cost. Renamed before the generic recursive copy so it routes through the ordinary field-copy path instead of recording an unmapped field and leaving the required variable_operation_cost absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.VARIABLE_OPERATION_COST_TYPES"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.VSC_SETPOINT_FIELDS","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 VSC dc_setpoint_* and ac_setpoint_* hold whichever quantity the control mode regulates; PSY6 has one field per quantity. An AC_VOLTAGE setpoint is instead the regulated bus's voltage_setpoint (_vsc_ac_voltage!).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.VSC_SETPOINT_FIELDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.VSC_SIDE_END","page":"Internals","text":"The end of a VSC line's arc each side's converter sits at.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.VSC_SIDE_END"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.WINDING_GROUP_ALPHA","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 WindingGroupNumber as the angle PSY6 keeps in TransformerCircuit.alpha (radians). A literal table, not -n * pi / 6: the enum is sparse and GROUP_1 is -30 degrees.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.WINDING_GROUP_ALPHA"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.Amperes","page":"Internals","text":"Current in A, where the schema declares kA.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.Amperes"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ArcEndVoltagePU","page":"Internals","text":"Per unit of the base voltage at one end of the component's arc (1 from, 2 to).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ArcEndVoltagePU"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.BusIndex","page":"Internals","text":"Bus voltage bases, arc endpoints and bus numbers of a PSY5 case: the bases convert impedances and voltages, the numbers resolve fields PSY5 names a bus by number.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.BusIndex"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.BusIndex-Tuple{AbstractDict{String, Float64}, AbstractDict{String, Tuple{String, String}}}","page":"Internals","text":"BusIndex(\n    base_voltage::AbstractDict{String, Float64},\n    arcs::AbstractDict{String, Tuple{String, String}}\n) -> PowerSystemsUpdater.BusIndex\n\n\nA BusIndex with voltage bases and arcs but no bus numbers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.BusIndex"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits","page":"Internals","text":"A component's PSY5 record and the bases needed to convert its fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.DCVoltageLimits","page":"Internals","text":"A VSC's DC voltage limits: RelativeTo rated_dc_voltage, but DC_VOLTAGE_NO_LIMIT stays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.DCVoltageLimits"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.DeviceBasePU","page":"Internals","text":"Per unit on the component's base_power (the system base if it has none).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.DeviceBasePU"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger","page":"Internals","text":"Maps PSY5 component UUIDs onto PSY6's document-wide integer ids, and records skipped components so references to them are detected rather than emitted dangling.\n\nowner: the component being translated (translate_component).\nunmapped: per component UUID, the PSY5 values with no PSY6 field, written to its ext (_carry_ext!).\nseries_refs: time series references deferred until the catalog assigns association ids (defer_series_ref!).\nbus_voltage_setpoints: by bus UUID, the setpoint a device gives the bus it regulates, written onto the buses at the end (_apply_bus_voltage_setpoints).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.Natural","page":"Internals","text":"Already in the physical unit PSY6 declares.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.Natural"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.NaturalPower","page":"Internals","text":"Natural power, which a per-unit PSY6 field takes on the component's base.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.NaturalPower"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.NonPhysicalBase","page":"Internals","text":"A value on a non-physical PSY5 base (a voltage of 0 or less), reported as an invalid value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.NonPhysicalBase"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PerHour","page":"Internals","text":"Natural, but per hour where PSY6 is per second.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PerHour"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.PiecewiseStepLayout","page":"Internals","text":"A PiecewiseStepData per timestep.\n\nPSY5 stored each as an (n, 2) matrix — hcat(x_coords, [NaN; y_coords]) — NaN-padded along its first axis to a common width and stacked. InfraStore stores the same value as one self-describing matrix row, so the padding has to be read off and the row rebuilt.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.PiecewiseStepLayout"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5ElementLayout","page":"Internals","text":"How PSY5 laid out one timestep's value, keyed by the data_type attribute it wrote beside the array.\n\nOnly the layouts the PSY5 corpus actually contains are mapped. An unmapped one errors: the two stores agree on plain scalars and on nothing else, so passing unknown bytes through would have InfraStore decode them as a different value with no complaint from either side.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5ElementLayout"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Storage","page":"Internals","text":"How PSY5 stored a field's value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Storage"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5TimeSeriesKind","page":"Internals","text":"Which of InfraStore's time series a PSY5 time_series_type becomes.\n\nDeterministicSingleTimeSeries is a stored array in PSY5 and a derivation in InfraStore: it shares its SingleTimeSeries' array and is re-described by InfraStore.transform_single_time_series!. So it stages nothing and is handled in _derive_forecasts! after every array is in the store.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5TimeSeriesKind"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.RelativeTo","page":"Internals","text":"A multiple of another PSY5 value, named by path in the record (e.g. a fraction of a limit).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.RelativeTo"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ScalarLayout","page":"Internals","text":"One scalar per timestep. The only layout the two formats already agree on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ScalarLayout"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.SeriesRef","page":"Internals","text":"A PSY5 time series key embedded in a field (FuelCurve.fuel_cost) of owner_uuid. Written as placeholder, a negative integer, until resolve_series_refs replaces it with the id of the association the key names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.SeriesRef"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.SystemBasePU","page":"Internals","text":"Per unit on the system base, whatever the component's own base.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.SystemBasePU"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.SystemBasePUOnVoltage","page":"Internals","text":"Per unit on the system base power and the kV at path in the record, not a bus's.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.SystemBasePUOnVoltage"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.UnknownStorage","page":"Internals","text":"PSY5 never annotated the field and it is not in PSY5_STORAGE.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.UnknownStorage"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.UnverifiedUnit","page":"Internals","text":"A value whose unit could not be established; see convert_units.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.UnverifiedUnit"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._accepts_absent-Tuple{Type}","page":"Internals","text":"_accepts_absent(field_type::Type) -> Bool\n\n\nWhether a model field is optional: the generator types it as a union with Absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._accepts_absent"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._add_service_associations_for!-Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_add_service_associations_for!(\n    doc::PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument,\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n)\n\n\nTurn raw's services list into one ServiceAssociation row per (service, entity). A skipped service is recorded as a cascaded skip; a skipped entity is already on the report.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._add_service_associations_for!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._add_supplemental_association!-Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, Int64, Int64, Type}","page":"Internals","text":"_add_supplemental_association!(\n    doc::PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument,\n    attribute_id::Int64,\n    owner_id::Int64,\n    attribute_model_type::Type\n)\n\n\nAdd only the association row for an attribute already added under another owner (IS shares one attribute among components); adding the model again would fail validate_document. Type names are PSY6's.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._add_supplemental_association!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._add_translated!-Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_add_translated!(\n    doc::PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument,\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n)\n\n\nTranslate raw, add the models to doc, and carry its ext across unless skipped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._add_translated!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._apply_bus_voltage_setpoints-Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}","page":"Internals","text":"_apply_bus_voltage_setpoints(\n    doc::PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger\n) -> PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument\n\n\ndoc with each bus's voltage_setpoint set from the setpoints recorded during translation (record_bus_voltage_setpoint!). Buses are translated before the converters that regulate them, so this runs afterwards through the document tree, as resolve_series_refs does.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._apply_bus_voltage_setpoints"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._band_from_fields-Tuple{AbstractDict, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"_band_from_fields(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    band::Symbol\n) -> Union{Nothing, Tuple{Dict{String, Any}, String}}\n\n\nA band from the transformer's own fields, with the PSY5 key it came from, or nothing: voltage_setpoint becomes a zero-width voltage band, tap_limits the tap-ratio band, and phase_angle_limits (radians) carries across.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._band_from_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._band_from_psse_ext-Tuple{AbstractDict, Symbol, Int64, AbstractString, Real}","page":"Internals","text":"_band_from_psse_ext(\n    ext::AbstractDict,\n    band::Symbol,\n    winding::Int64,\n    objective::AbstractString,\n    base_power::Real\n) -> Union{Nothing, Dict{String, Any}}\n\n\nA band from the PSS/E columns kept in ext, for winding winding, or nothing when they are absent or their COD disagrees with the objective.\n\nVMI/VMA are the target band: per unit voltage, or MVAr/MW converted to per unit on base_power. RMI/RMA are the actuator band: tap ratio, or a phase shifter's angle limits in degrees.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._band_from_psse_ext"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._band_from_psy5_default-Tuple{AbstractDict, Symbol, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_band_from_psy5_default(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    band::Symbol,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Union{Nothing, Dict{String, Any}}\n\n\nThe voltage band of a TapTransformer whose older file omits voltage_setpoint, from PSY5's own default, or nothing. Recorded as a PSY5 default.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._band_from_psy5_default"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._build_circuit-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext, Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"_build_circuit(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext,\n    alpha::Float64\n) -> Tuple{PowerOperationsOpenAPIModels.TransformerCircuit, Vector{String}}\n\n\nBuild a two-winding transformer's TransformerCircuit, and the PSY5 keys its bands used.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._build_circuit"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._carry_ext!-Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_carry_ext!(\n    doc::PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument,\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n)\n\n\nCarry raw's PSY5 ext, plus the values translation kept (keep_unmapped!, under UNMAPPED_EXT_KEY), into doc.ext by PSY6 id. A transformer's entry goes on the transformer, not its circuits, which have no ext.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._carry_ext!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._check_no_time_series_pointers!-Tuple{AbstractDict, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"_check_no_time_series_pointers!(\n    value::AbstractDict,\n    owner_type::Union{Nothing, AbstractString}\n)\n\n\nThrows Psy5FormatError if any immediate child of value is a time-series pointer. owner_type is value's own PSY5 type name, so the message names the field as Owner.field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._check_no_time_series_pointers!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._check_transformer3w_top_level!-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_check_transformer3w_top_level!(raw::AbstractDict)\n\n\nCircuits take rating from rating_$suffix (PSY5 default 0.0) and the top-level rating is dropped, so a non-zero top-level rating with a zero winding rating would silently give a zero-capacity circuit: error instead.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._check_transformer3w_top_level!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._control_block-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Int64, Real, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_control_block(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    objective_key::AbstractString,\n    winding::Int64,\n    base_power::Real,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Tuple{Any, Dict{Symbol, Any}, Vector{String}}\n\n\nThe control_objective, its bands, and the PSY5 keys used, for one circuit.\n\nEach band in CONTROL_OBJECTIVE_BANDS (and tap_ratio_limits for TAP_MOVING_OBJECTIVES) is taken from the PSY5 fields (_band_from_fields), else PSS/E ext (_band_from_psse_ext), else PSY5's default (_band_from_psy5_default). If a required band is in none, the circuit gets UNDEFINED so the document stays valid, and the objective is reported and kept in ext.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._control_block"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._decode_kwargs-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, AbstractDict{Symbol}}} where T<:InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel","page":"Internals","text":"_decode_kwargs(\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel},\n    kwargs::AbstractDict{Symbol}\n) -> Dict{Symbol, Any}\n\n\nDecode every value in kwargs against T's own declared field type.\n\nThe PSY5->PSY6 translation pipeline stages plain Julia values — JSON-shaped nested Dicts built by translate_value, bare enum spellings as String (\"COMPONENT_BASE\", \"UP\", ...), resolved reference ids as Int — that the OpenAPI 1.1 generator's strictly typed, immutable structs do not accept as-is: the old 0.2 generator's untyped fields tolerated them, but a field like power_units::UnitSystem or shut_down::InputOutputCurve now rejects a bare String/Dict with a MethodError. ICOM.decode is the generated packages' public entry point for this (the runtime's _decode, under the name every consumer is meant to call), so this routes every hand-built kwarg through the one path that already knows how to turn a raw value into T's declared type, whatever shape that type is.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._decode_kwargs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._defer_series_refs-Tuple{AbstractDict, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}","page":"Internals","text":"_defer_series_refs(\n    value::AbstractDict,\n    owner_type::Union{Nothing, AbstractString},\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger\n) -> AbstractDict\n\n\nvalue with each embedded series key in SERIES_REF_FIELDS moved to its PSY6 field as a placeholder, resolved once the catalog exists (resolve_series_refs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._defer_series_refs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_commitment_mode-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, AbstractDict}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"_derive_commitment_mode(\n    _::Type{T},\n    raw::AbstractDict\n) -> Any\n\n\nPSY5 must_run = true is commitment_mode = MUST_RUN; false is PSY6's default.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_commitment_mode"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_fields-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"_derive_fields(\n    _::Type{T},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Any\n\n\nRewrite PSY5 fields into the different PSY6 fields that carry the same information. Each consumes the PSY5 field it maps; one that cannot be mapped is left for the copy to report.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_forecasts!-Tuple{InfraStore.Store, AbstractVector{<:AbstractDict}}","page":"Internals","text":"_derive_forecasts!(\n    store::InfraStore.Store,\n    rows::AbstractVector{<:AbstractDict}\n)\n\n\nRe-derive the DeterministicSingleTimeSeries rows as InfraStore derivations.\n\nInfraStore.transform_single_time_series! works on every SingleTimeSeries of one owner category at a resolution at once, so it can only reproduce a PSY5 sidecar whose derived rows cover all of them. Both preconditions are checked before anything is written — one (horizon, interval) per category and resolution, and one derived row per static row — and a sidecar that breaks either aborts rather than silently gaining or losing forecasts.\n\nOnly components get derived forecasts, as in IS (owner_category = InfraStore.Component): a supplemental attribute's static series must not gain one.\n\nnormalize_single_window and require_uniform_forecast_grid are set the way IS sets them, because IS is what reads the result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_forecasts!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_minimum_energy_offer-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_derive_minimum_energy_offer(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Any\n\n\nPSY5 MarketBidCost.no_load_cost (h) is PSY6 minimum_energy_offer (/MWh at minimum power): no_load_cost / P_min, with Pmin the device's `activepowerlimits.min` in MW. With no positive Pmin the cost is left for the copy to report.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._derive_minimum_energy_offer"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._features-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_features(row::AbstractDict) -> Dict{String, Any}\n\n\nA row's features as PSY6 stores them, reserved names renamed by _psy6_feature_name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._features"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._head_to_volume_factor-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_head_to_volume_factor(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Any\n\n\nPSY6's head_to_volume_factor is a bare FunctionData; PSY5 wraps it one level deeper in an InputOutputCurve. A non-null input_at_zero has no destination in the unwrap, so it is recorded and kept in the reservoir's ext rather than dropped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._head_to_volume_factor"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._impedance_correction_curve-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_impedance_correction_curve(raw::AbstractDict) -> Any\n\n\nPSY5 ImpedanceCorrectionData.impedance_correction_curve becomes the PSY6 field named for its transformer_control_mode. A phase-shift curve's x axis is degrees in PSY5, radians in PSY6.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._impedance_correction_curve"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._in_declared_units-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, Symbol, AbstractString, Any, PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, ConversionReport}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"_in_declared_units(\n    _::Type{T},\n    field::Symbol,\n    key::AbstractString,\n    value,\n    units::PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits,\n    kwargs::AbstractDict,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    report::ConversionReport\n) -> Tuple{Any, Bool}\n\n\n(value, write): value converted to the unit T declares for field, and whether to write it. The chosen unit basis goes into kwargs. A value that could not be converted is reported; an optional field is then left unset (PSY5 value kept in ext), a required one written as stored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._in_declared_units"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._is_start_up_stages_shape-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_start_up_stages_shape(dict::AbstractDict) -> Bool\n\n\nStartUpStages carries no __metadata__ tag in PSY5, so it is detected by its unique key set instead, the same way is_reference classifies by shape rather than by tag.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._is_start_up_stages_shape"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._lcc_control-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_lcc_control(raw::AbstractDict) -> Any\n\n\nPSY5 LCC power_mode and transfer_setpoint become PSY6 control_mode and one setpoint: POWER with power_transfer_setpoint (MW), or CURRENT with current_transfer_setpoint (A).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._lcc_control"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._legacy_array-Tuple{HDF5.File, AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_legacy_array(\n    file::HDF5.File,\n    row::AbstractDict\n) -> Tuple{Any, PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5ElementLayout}\n\n\nThe stored array for an association, together with the layout of one of its timesteps.\n\nA row naming an array the sidecar does not hold aborts the conversion: PSY6 resolves time series through the catalog this pass writes, so an association with no array behind it would read back as a series whose values silently went missing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._legacy_array"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._magnetizing_shunt-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_magnetizing_shunt(\n    raw::AbstractDict\n) -> Union{Nothing, InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.ComplexNumber}\n\n\nPSY5 primary_shunt (real/imag) as PSY6's magnetizing_shunt ComplexNumber.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._magnetizing_shunt"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._may_leave_unset-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, Symbol, AbstractString}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"_may_leave_unset(\n    _::Type{T},\n    field::Symbol,\n    key::AbstractString\n) -> Bool\n\n\nWhether a value that could not be converted may be left unset rather than written.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._may_leave_unset"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._milliseconds-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_milliseconds(period::AbstractDict) -> Any\n\n\nMilliseconds in a PSY5 period ({\"value\": 1, \"type\": \"Hour\"}) or an ISO 8601 duration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._milliseconds"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._multiplier_quantity_kind-Tuple{Nothing}","page":"Internals","text":"_multiplier_quantity_kind(_::Nothing)\n\n\nThe quantity_kind a multiplier names, or nothing when this translator cannot determine one. Shared by the document row and the InfraStore catalog row, which must agree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._multiplier_quantity_kind"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._non_physical_base-Tuple{AbstractString, Real}","page":"Internals","text":"_non_physical_base(key::AbstractString, value::Real) -> Any\n\n\nWhether value is a non-physical base voltage for a transformer winding (base_voltage_*) or VSC rated_dc_voltage. PSY5 accepts 0.0, PSY6 needs a positive base; build_kwargs leaves such a value unset and reports it.\n\nA bus base_voltage is excluded: PowerSystems 6's Line check cannot handle an unset one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._non_physical_base"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._normalize_power_units-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_normalize_power_units(\n    value::AbstractString\n) -> AbstractString\n\n\nPSY5 spells the per-unit basis DEVICE_BASE; PSY6's UnitSystem enum only has COMPONENT_BASE/NATURAL_UNITS. Normalizes a nested power_units key (CostCurve, LossCurve, …) wherever one is found on a translated dict — the top-level component power_units bypasses this entirely, since direct_translate always sets it directly to \"COMPONENT_BASE\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._normalize_power_units"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._operational_state-Tuple{Bool}","page":"Internals","text":"_operational_state(status::Bool) -> String\n\n\nPSY5 spells the initial commitment state as a plain Bool on the device types that carry a status field of PSY6's OperationalStates enum (ThermalStandard, ThermalMultiStart, HybridSystem, HydroDispatch, HydroTurbine; HydroPumpTurbine's status key means something else — see its own translate method). PSY5 has no STARTUP/SHUTDOWN concept, so true/false map onto the two states it can express.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._operational_state"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._per_unit_factor-Tuple{AbstractString, Real, PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits}","page":"Internals","text":"_per_unit_factor(\n    unit::AbstractString,\n    base::Real,\n    units::PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits\n) -> Any\n\n\nThe factor from per unit on base MVA to unit, or nothing if not reachable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._per_unit_factor"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._physical_base_voltage-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_physical_base_voltage(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    key::AbstractString,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Any\n\n\nraw[key] if it is a physical base voltage; otherwise nothing, reported and kept in ext as build_kwargs does (_non_physical_base).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._physical_base_voltage"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._psy5_duration-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_psy5_duration(text::AbstractString) -> Any\n\n\nDecode one PSY5 duration string into the Dates.Period InfraStore's writers take.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._psy5_duration"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._psy5_features-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_psy5_features(row::AbstractDict) -> Dict{String, Any}\n\n\nA row's PSY5 features as a dictionary. PSY5 stores them as a JSON list of one-pair objects ([{\"year\":2024}]) with Bool, Int or String values, the encoding IS3's reader expects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._psy5_features"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._psy6_feature_name-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_psy6_feature_name(name::AbstractString) -> Any\n\n\nA PSY5 feature name as PSY6 stores it: a reserved name gets _feature appended.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._psy6_feature_name"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._quantity_kind-Tuple{Nothing, AbstractDict, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"_quantity_kind(\n    _::Nothing,\n    _::AbstractDict,\n    _::ConversionReport\n)\n\n\nquantity_kind for a row's multiplier. A row with no multiplier declares no quantity and reports nothing; one whose accessor names no determinable quantity is reported.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._quantity_kind"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._record_dropped_fields!-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext, AbstractSet{String}, AbstractVector{String}}","page":"Internals","text":"_record_dropped_fields!(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext,\n    known::AbstractSet{String},\n    consumed::AbstractVector{String}\n)\n\n\nReport and keep in ext every PSY5 key of raw that is not internal, in known, or in consumed. Translation reads only the keys it knows, so without this the rest would vanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._record_dropped_fields!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._record_feature_renames!-Tuple{AbstractDict, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"_record_feature_renames!(\n    row::AbstractDict,\n    report::ConversionReport\n)\n\n\nWarn about and report each feature _features renames on row.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._record_feature_renames!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._record_time_series_skips!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"_record_time_series_skips!(\n    case::PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    report::ConversionReport\n)\n\n\nRecord on report the time series lost with skipped owners. The document's association rows come from convert_time_series reading back the sidecar, not from here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._record_time_series_skips!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._record_unmapped_nested_fields!-Tuple{AbstractDict, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"_record_unmapped_nested_fields!(\n    translated::AbstractDict,\n    type_name::Union{Nothing, AbstractString},\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    report::ConversionReport\n)\n\n\nRecord every key on a resolved nested composite (type_name from __metadata__.type, or \"StartUpStages\" for the untagged shape) that is not one of ICOM.model_type(type_name)'s fieldnames — the nested analogue of build_kwargs's unmapped-field guard. The value is kept in the owner's ext as Type.field.\n\nOnly fires when type_name resolves to a registered PSY6 model; an unresolved nested dict (no __metadata__.type, or a PSY5 type with no PSY6 counterpart) is forwarded unchanged, as before, with nothing to check its keys against. __metadata__ itself is never flagged: the schemas allow the extra key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._record_unmapped_nested_fields!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._regulated_bus_fields-Tuple{AbstractDict, Any, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_regulated_bus_fields(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    objective,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Dict{Symbol, Any}\n\n\nPSY5 regulated_bus_number (PSS/E CONT) as regulated_bus (an id) and regulated_bus_orientation. PSS/E holds the orientation in the sign: positive is TO (winding two side), negative FROM. It is stated only for a bus off the arc, else UNDEFINED.\n\n0 means none. Under an objective outside REGULATED_BUS_OBJECTIVES the number has no PSY6 field, so it is kept in ext and reported.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._regulated_bus_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._required_duration-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_required_duration(\n    row::AbstractDict,\n    key::AbstractString\n) -> Any\n\n\nThe duration in a required association column, which is missing on rows whose type has no use for it (a SingleTimeSeries carries no horizon). A row that needs one and has none is malformed, not defaulted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._required_duration"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._scaling_factor_multiplier-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_scaling_factor_multiplier(row::AbstractDict) -> Any\n\n\nPSY5's scaling_factor_multiplier column holds either NULL or InfrastructureSystems's serialized-Function marker ({\"__metadata__\":{\"module\":...,\"function\":...}}). The marker is decoded to the bare accessor name (get_max_active_power); the PowerSystems. module prefix it carries is dropped because the name is read as a label here, never resolved to a function — this package deliberately does not depend on PowerSystems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._scaling_factor_multiplier"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._series_association_id-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.SeriesRef, Any, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}","page":"Internals","text":"_series_association_id(\n    ref::PowerSystemsUpdater.SeriesRef,\n    rows,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger\n) -> Any\n\n\nThe id of the one association row matching a deferred SeriesRef: same owner, name, kind, features and, if the key gives one, resolution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._series_association_id"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._settle-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.NonPhysicalBase, Type{T}, Symbol, AbstractString, Any, PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, ConversionReport}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"_settle(\n    _::PowerSystemsUpdater.NonPhysicalBase,\n    _::Type{T},\n    field::Symbol,\n    key::AbstractString,\n    value,\n    units::PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    report::ConversionReport\n) -> Tuple{Any, Bool}\n\n\nA value on a non-physical base is reported as an invalid value; handled like UnverifiedUnit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._settle"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._stage_time_series!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.SingleKind, InfraStore.AddBatch, HDF5.File, AbstractDict, Int64, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"_stage_time_series!(\n    _::PowerSystemsUpdater.SingleKind,\n    batch::InfraStore.AddBatch,\n    file::HDF5.File,\n    row::AbstractDict,\n    owner_id::Int64,\n    report::ConversionReport\n)\n\n\nStage one association's array onto batch.\n\nunits, quantity_kind and unit_system are the same three declarations the document's TimeSeriesAssociation carries, written into the catalog because that is the copy PSY6's importer reads: it adopts the sidecar's catalog as the System's store rather than replaying the document's rows. InfraStore has always spelled it quantity_kind, so unlike the document side this needs no rename.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._stage_time_series!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._static_values-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.ScalarLayout, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Internals","text":"_static_values(\n    _::PowerSystemsUpdater.ScalarLayout,\n    data::AbstractVector{<:Real}\n) -> Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Nothing}\n\n\nValues for a static series: the array as stored plus the element_type tag InfraStore keys reconstruction on, or nothing for plain scalars of the array's own element type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._static_values"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._store_supplemental_associations-Tuple{AbstractVector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.SupplementalAttributeAssociation}}","page":"Internals","text":"_store_supplemental_associations(\n    rows::AbstractVector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.SupplementalAttributeAssociation}\n) -> Any\n\n\nThe document's supplemental attribute associations as catalog rows. The catalog must hold them all already: under time_series_read_only PSY6 cannot add the ones it lacks.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._store_supplemental_associations"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._store_unit_system-Tuple{Nothing}","page":"Internals","text":"_store_unit_system(_::Nothing)\n\n\nThe basis InfraStore records for values a PSY5 multiplier normalized — the store's own spelling of the COMPONENT_BASE the document's association row declares: a multiplier means the values are per-unit on the owner's own base.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._store_unit_system"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._time_series_kind-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_time_series_kind(\n    row::AbstractDict\n) -> PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5TimeSeriesKind\n\n\nProbabilistic and Scenarios are deliberately unmapped: their percentiles and scenario count live on the PSY5 metadata object, not in the association table this package reads, so neither can be reconstructed from a row and neither appears in the PSY5 corpus. Erroring names what is missing instead of writing a forecast with invented parameters.\n\nNonSequentialTimeSeries is absent for a different reason, and its absence is correct rather than pending: it exists only in the psy6 line, so no PSY5 system can contain one and there is nothing to convert into one. Do not add a kind for it — a row naming it would mean the input is not a PSY5 system, which this error should report.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._time_series_kind"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._vsc_ac_voltage!-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractDict, AbstractString, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_vsc_ac_voltage!(\n    derived::AbstractDict,\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    side::AbstractString,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> AbstractDict\n\n\nMove one AC_VOLTAGE converter end of a PSY5 VSC line onto derived in PSY6's form. PSY5 names the regulated bus by number (remote_bus_control_<side>, 0 for its own terminal) with the target in ac_setpoint_<side>; PSY6 names a remote bus by id (remote_regulated_bus_<side>) and keeps the target on that bus (_apply_bus_voltage_setpoints).\n\nA remote bus number that no ACBus has is a dangling source reference: the number and setpoint are kept in ext and reported as dropped invalid values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._vsc_ac_voltage!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._warn_switched_admittance_approximations-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"_warn_switched_admittance_approximations(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n)\n\n\nReport and log the SwitchedAdmittances the mapping does not reproduce:\n\nsolved_admittance: Y is non-zero and a block is in service. PSY5 takes Y + Σ initial_status · Y_increase; PSY6 takes Y alone.\nnumber_engaged: an in-service block has several steps, but initial_status does not say how many are engaged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._warn_switched_admittance_approximations"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._winding_alpha-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_winding_alpha(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    suffix::AbstractString\n) -> Any\n\n\nA winding's phase shift: α_$suffix (radians) if present, else its group number's angle.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._winding_alpha"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._winding_available-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_winding_available(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    suffix::AbstractString\n) -> Any\n\n\nA winding circuit's availability: the transformer's available AND available_$suffix. PSY6 derives the transformer's availability from its circuits.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._winding_available"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._window_count-Tuple{AbstractDict, Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"_window_count(row::AbstractDict, from_array::Integer) -> Any\n\n\nThe window count a Deterministic row declares, checked against the array behind it.\n\nA disagreement means the row and the array describe different forecasts, and the store would take the count on faith — so it aborts rather than writing a forecast whose windows do not line up with its metadata.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._window_count"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._window_values-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.ScalarLayout, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"Internals","text":"_window_values(\n    _::PowerSystemsUpdater.ScalarLayout,\n    data::AbstractMatrix{<:Real}\n) -> Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, Nothing}\n\n\nValues for a dense Deterministic: (horizon_count, window_count) for scalars, and (horizon_count, window_count, k) once a row-encoded element gains its own axis — the same shapes InfraStore.Deterministic takes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._window_values"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._with_rating_from_limits-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"_with_rating_from_limits(raw::AbstractDict) -> Any\n\n\nPSY6 requires a rating on the generic and LCC HVDC lines. PSY5 has none, so it is active_power_limits_from.max (same base). active_power_limits_from stays for build_kwargs to report as dropped: its min and the _to limits have no PSY6 field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._with_rating_from_limits"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater._zero_offer_curve-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"_zero_offer_curve() -> Dict{String, Any}\n\n\nThe empty offer curve, mirroring PSY6's own ZERO_OFFER_CURVE (PowerSystems/src/models/cost_functions/MarketBidCost.jl): a CostCurve over a PiecewiseIncrementalCurve(0.0, [0.0, 0.0], [0.0]) in natural units with zero VOM. Unlike the fields above, Core/common.json documents no default here, so the sanction is PSY's constructor default rather than the schema's — the same value any PSY6 caller that omits the field already gets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater._zero_offer_curve"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.all_components-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case}","page":"Internals","text":"all_components(\n    case::PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case\n) -> Base.Iterators.Flatten{I} where I<:Tuple{Any, Any}\n\n\nEvery raw component case carries, masked ones first. assign_id! order matters and is not this order — build_document walks components/masked_components separately for that — but callers that only look a component up by uuid can use this.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.all_components"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.allocate_id!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}","page":"Internals","text":"allocate_id!(ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger) -> Int64\n\n\nReserve an id for a component translation synthesizes, such as a transformer circuit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.allocate_id!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.arc_end_voltage-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits, Int64}","page":"Internals","text":"arc_end_voltage(\n    units::PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits,\n    end_index::Int64\n) -> Union{Nothing, Float64}\n\n\nThe base voltage (kV) of one end of the component's arc (1 from, 2 to), or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.arc_end_voltage"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.assign_id!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"assign_id!(\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    uuid::AbstractString\n) -> Int64\n\n\nAssign an id to uuid, or return the one already assigned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.assign_id!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.base_power_for-Tuple{AbstractDict, Real}","page":"Internals","text":"base_power_for(raw::AbstractDict, system_base::Real) -> Any\n\n\nThe base power to record on a PSY6 component.\n\nPSY5 stores values in device base, but leaves the base implicit for components that declare no base_power field (Line, ACBus, Arc, Area, LoadZone, …) — those ride on the system base. PSY6 requires it recorded per component, so supply the system base there. No value is ever rescaled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.base_power_for"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.build_document-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"build_document(\n    case::PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case,\n    report::ConversionReport\n) -> Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}\n\n\nAssemble a PSY6 SystemDocument from a PSY5 case: first assign every component an id so references resolve in any order, then translate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.build_document"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.build_kwargs-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, ConversionReport}} where T<:InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel","page":"Internals","text":"build_kwargs(\n    ::Type{T<:InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    report::ConversionReport;\n    extra,\n    units\n) -> Dict{Symbol, Any}\n\n\nBuild the keyword arguments for T from a PSY5 component dict.\n\nCopies by name for every field T declares, resolving UUID references to integer ids. PSY5 keys with no counterpart on T are recorded on report rather than dropped silently — an unmapped field is a finding about the schemas.\n\nWith units, each value is first converted to the unit the schema declares (convert_units) and the chosen unit-basis field is written (admittance_units, ...). Without it, values are copied as stored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.build_kwargs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.bus_id_for_number-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext, Integer, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"bus_id_for_number(\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext,\n    number::Integer,\n    context::AbstractString\n) -> Int64\n\n\nThe PSY6 id of the ACBus numbered number; context names the field in the error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.bus_id_for_number"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.bus_number-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"bus_number(\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext,\n    uuid::AbstractString\n) -> Int64\n\n\nThe number of the PSY5 ACBus whose UUID is uuid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.bus_number"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.component_units-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"component_units(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits\n\n\nThe bases convert_units needs for raw.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.component_units"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.component_uuid-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"component_uuid(raw::AbstractDict) -> String\n\n\nThe UUID PSY5 uses to reference this component.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.component_uuid"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.convert_time_series-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, AbstractString, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"convert_time_series(\n    case::PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    out_dir::AbstractString,\n    report::ConversionReport;\n    supplemental_associations\n) -> Tuple{String, Any}\n\n\nRewrite case's PSY5 sidecar as the InfraStore pair PSY6 reads: out_dir/time_series.h5 holding the content-addressed arrays and out_dir/time_series.h5.sqlite holding the catalog. Returns the .h5 path (what the document names) together with the InfrastructureTimeSeriesOpenAPIModels.TimeSeriesAssociation rows read back from the freshly written catalog.\n\nThe two files are one artifact — the arrays are addressed by content hash and the catalog is the only thing that says which association each hash belongs to — so they must travel together.\n\nThe returned rows, not a document-side re-derivation of the PSY5 rows, are what the caller must add to the document: they carry the uri/data_hash/element_type/element_shape the store itself computed, so they are guaranteed to match what PSY6's importer will find in the catalog. Rows whose owner was skipped are left out; their loss is recorded by _record_time_series_skips!, which walks the same PSY5 rows to build the document.\n\nsupplemental_associations are the document's supplemental attribute association rows, written into the catalog as well (see _store_supplemental_associations).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.convert_time_series"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.convert_units-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Storage, Nothing, Any, PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits}","page":"Internals","text":"convert_units(\n    _::PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Storage,\n    _::Nothing,\n    value,\n    _::PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits\n) -> Any\n\n\nvalue (as PSY5 stored it) in the unit PSY6 declares (unit, from target_unit), or an UnverifiedUnit or NonPhysicalBase when that cannot be established.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.convert_units"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.defer_series_ref!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"defer_series_ref!(\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    key::AbstractDict\n) -> Int64\n\n\nDefer an embedded time series key, returning the placeholder to write in its place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.defer_series_ref!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.direct_translate-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}} where T<:InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel","page":"Internals","text":"direct_translate(\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Vector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel}\n\n\nBuild one PSY6 model of type T by copying raw's fields by name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.direct_translate"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.keep_unmapped!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, AbstractString, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"keep_unmapped!(\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    key::AbstractString,\n    value\n)\n\n\nKeep value, a PSY5 value with no PSY6 field, on the component being translated under key (the field name, or Type.field for a nested struct). Callers also record the field on the report. A nothing value, or no owner outside translate_component, keeps nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.keep_unmapped!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.lookup_id-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"lookup_id(\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    uuid::AbstractString\n) -> Int64\n\n\nResolve uuid to its id; every reference resolution goes through here. Throws for a skipped or unknown uuid, backstopping references_skipped, whose check is shallow.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.lookup_id"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.masked_components-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case}","page":"Internals","text":"masked_components(case::PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case) -> Any\n\n\nHybridSystem sub-units (thermal_unit/renewable_unit/storage/electric_load), which PSY5 excludes from components(case) but PSY6 treats as ordinary referenced components.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.masked_components"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.openapi_type-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"openapi_type(name::Symbol) -> Any\n\n\nThe OpenAPI model type named name, from whichever model package defines it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.openapi_type"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.owner_translated-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, AbstractDict}","page":"Internals","text":"owner_translated(\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    row::AbstractDict\n) -> Bool\n\n\nWhether a row's owner survived translation, and so whether the row can be carried across at all. Both the document's association rows and the InfraStore catalog's are filtered through this, so the two always describe the same set of series.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.owner_translated"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.psy5_storage-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"psy5_storage(\n    psy5_type::AbstractString,\n    field::AbstractString\n) -> PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Storage\n\n\nHow PSY5 stored field on psy5_type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.psy5_storage"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.read_associations-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"read_associations(h5_path::AbstractString) -> Vector\n\n\nRead PSY5's time_series_associations table.\n\nIS.from_h5_file cannot be used: it reconstructs a TimeSeriesMetadataStore, which deserializes scaling_factor_multiplier into a live Function and so requires PowerSystems to be loaded. This package must not depend on it. Only the raw rows are needed, so IS's byte extraction is replicated and the SQLite file queried directly.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.read_associations"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.read_psy5-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"read_psy5(\n    path::AbstractString\n) -> PowerSystemsUpdater.Psy5Case\n\n\nRead a PSY5 to_json bundle. path is the extensionless system file; the HDF5 sidecar is located by PSY5's own naming rule (splitext(basename) + _time_series_storage.h5).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.read_psy5"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.record_bus_voltage_setpoint!-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext, AbstractString, Real, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"record_bus_voltage_setpoint!(\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext,\n    bus_uuid::AbstractString,\n    setpoint::Real,\n    source::AbstractString\n)\n\n\nRecord setpoint as the voltage_setpoint of bus bus_uuid, for _apply_bus_voltage_setpoints. PSY6 has one setpoint per bus: a second, different one is reported as an approximate mapping and the first kept.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.record_bus_voltage_setpoint!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.references_skipped-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}","page":"Internals","text":"references_skipped(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger\n) -> Bool\n\n\nTrue when any reference on raw points at a skipped component, which must then be skipped too (validate_document does not check references). Dynamic model links are never written, so they do not count.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.references_skipped"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.resolve_series_refs-Tuple{PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_series_refs(\n    doc::PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger\n) -> PowerCoreOpenAPIModels.SystemDocument\n\n\ndoc with each deferred SeriesRef placeholder replaced by its association id. The catalog that mints the ids is written after the components, so the document is rebuilt from its tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.resolve_series_refs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.target_unit-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, Symbol, AbstractDict}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"target_unit(\n    _::Type{T},\n    field::Symbol,\n    raw::AbstractDict\n) -> Union{Tuple{Any, Nothing}, Tuple{Any, Pair{_A, String} where _A}}\n\n\n(unit, discriminator => basis) PSY6 declares for field of T; either is nothing when absent or when the updater need not write the basis. A per-unit basis is preferred, since PSY5's device-base values already are per unit on base_power. A data discriminator is read from raw; any other falls back to its first power-unit basis.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.target_unit"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate-Tuple{Val{:MonitoredLine}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"translate(\n    _::Val{:MonitoredLine},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Vector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel}\n\n\nPSY6 has no MonitoredLine: it is a Line with operational_flow_limit set. PSY5's flow_limits holds one maximum per direction; each becomes that direction's max with a min of 0.0. The limits share rating's base, so they are not scaled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate-Tuple{Val{:PhaseShiftingTransformer3W}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"translate(\n    _::Val{:PhaseShiftingTransformer3W},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Vector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel}\n\n\nPSY6 has no phase-shifting three-winding type: each circuit carries its own alpha. A PhaseShiftingTransformer3W differs only by α_$suffix per winding, so it translates as a Transformer3W.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate-Tuple{Val{:SwitchedAdmittance}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"translate(\n    _::Val{:SwitchedAdmittance},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Vector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel}\n\n\nPSY5 SwitchedAdmittance, mapped as PowerFlowFileParser's PSS/E reader maps the same record (PowerFlowFileParser.jl/src/openapi/shunt.jl):\n\nY (BINIT) -> solved_admittance, its susceptance, unset when zero. A non-zero conductance has no PSY6 field, so Y is then kept in ext whole.\ninitial_status (per-block in-service flag) -> number_engaged (per-block step count).\nY_increase -> y_increase; admittance_limits -> the field of SWITCHED_ADMITTANCE_LIMITS_FIELD, else ext.\nregulated_bus_number -> remote_regulated_bus (an id); 0 or the shunt's own bus is none.\n\nKnown inexact mappings are reported (_warn_switched_admittance_approximations).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate-Tuple{Val{:Transformer3W}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"translate(\n    _::Val{:Transformer3W},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Vector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel}\n\n\nPSY5 stores both the pairwise and the star-equivalent forms, so nothing is inverted. PSY5's 1-3 pair is PSY6's 3-1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate-Union{Tuple{S}, Tuple{Val{S}, AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}} where S","page":"Internals","text":"translate(\n    _::Val{S},\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Vector{InfrastructureCoreOpenAPIModels.APIModel}\n\n\nFallback for a PSY5 type with no PSY6 counterpart: skip and record.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate_component-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext}","page":"Internals","text":"translate_component(\n    raw::AbstractDict,\n    ctx::PowerSystemsUpdater.TranslationContext\n) -> Any\n\n\nTranslate one PSY5 component into zero or more PSY6 models. Zero models means it was skipped, and the reason is already on the report and the ledger.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate_component"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.translate_value-Tuple{AbstractDict, PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger, ConversionReport}","page":"Internals","text":"translate_value(\n    value::AbstractDict,\n    ledger::PowerSystemsUpdater.Ledger,\n    report::ConversionReport\n) -> Union{Int64, Dict{String, Any}}\n\n\nNon-reference dicts are forwarded recursively rather than verbatim, so a nested oneOf (a CostCurve containing a ValueCurve containing FunctionData) gets its discriminator at every level in one pass. __metadata__ is left in place: the schemas allow the extra key.\n\nA key whose PSY5 value is nothing is dropped rather than forwarded as JSON null, matching build_kwargs's top-level behavior: PSY6 optional fields (input_at_zero, and similar) are typed without null, so a present-but-null key fails schema validation where an absent key decodes to ABSENT.\n\nEvery resolved nested composite is also checked against its PSY6 fieldnames (_record_unmapped_nested_fields!), the same guard build_kwargs applies at the top level — otherwise a PSY5 field with no PSY6 counterpart inside a nested object (for example FuelCurve.startup_fuel_offtake) would be forwarded into the output silently instead of being recorded as a finding.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.translate_value"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#PowerSystemsUpdater.voltage_base-Tuple{PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits}","page":"Internals","text":"voltage_base(\n    units::PowerSystemsUpdater.ComponentUnits\n) -> Union{Nothing, Float64}\n\n\nThe component's voltage base (kV) from its bus or its arc's from bus, or nothing. Transformers, whose ends differ, have per-unit impedances that are never converted here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.voltage_base"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#What-changes-between-PSY5-and-PSY6","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"Everything a serialized PSY5 component meets on the way to a PSY6 SystemDocument. Derived from converting 104 real systems; each row is something the converter had to handle, not something the schema merely permits.","title":"What changes between PSY5 and PSY6"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Identity-and-references","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":" PSY5 PSY6\nIdentity internal.uuid.value (UUID) id, an integer\nReference {\"value\": \"<uuid>\"} the target's integer id\nUniqueness per system across all types, and disjoint from supplemental-attribute ids\n\nA bus number is not an id. Nothing in PSY6 validates ordinary component references (bus, arc), so a converter must guarantee them itself — validate_document checks only association, owner and ext keys.","title":"Identity and references"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Units","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"PSY5 offers SYSTEM_BASE, DEVICE_BASE, NATURAL_UNITS. PSY6 drops SYSTEM_BASE.\n\nStored PSY5 values are already device base — _get_multiplier(…, ::Val{DEVICE_BASE}, ::Any) = 1.0, with the other two derived at access time. So no rescaling is needed to emit DEVICE_BASE.\n\nPSY6 now records base_power on Line, MonitoredLine, and ten other components whose base is the system base (Area, LoadZone, FixedAdmittance, AreaInterchange, DiscreteControlledACBranch, GenericArcImpedance, TransmissionInterface, and the three TwoTerminal*Line HVDC types — see the BasePowerKind trait in PowerSystems' src/models/components.jl), recorded per component \"in lieu of a system-level table\". ACBus, Arc, AGC, and DCBus still declare none; their base remains implicit on the system base.","title":"Units"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Converting-each-field-into-its-declared-unit","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"Not every field is per unit in PSY6. The schema declares a unit for each field (x-unit): either through a basis field with a per-unit option (power_units, parameter_units), a basis field without one (admittance_units: S or MVAr; energy_units: MWh), a data field (level_data_type: m³, m or MWh), or outright (reserve requirement is MW, LCC impedances are ohm). The updater converts every field it writes by one rule (src/translate/units.jl):\n\nPSY6 side: the unit the schema declares, read from the model packages (unit_discriminator, declared_unit). A per-unit basis is chosen wherever one exists, and any basis the conversion chose is written (admittance_units = COMPONENT_MVAR, ...).\nPSY5 side: how PSY5 stored the field. Fields PSY5's descriptors mark needs_conversion are device-base per unit; that table is generated (src/translate/psy5_units_generated.jl, by scripts/psy5_units/generate_psy5_units.jl). Fields PSY5 stored some other way without saying so are listed by hand in PSY5_STORAGE: system-base per unit (reserve requirement, FixedAdmittance.Y, LCC impedances), relative to another value (reservoir levels as a fraction of storage_level_limits.max; VSC DC voltage limits in per unit of rated_dc_voltage), per hour where PSY6 is per second (reservoir flows), or already natural (bases, LCC kV fields).\nConversion: a per-unit PSY6 unit takes PSY5's device-base value as is. A power unit (MW, MVA, MVAr, MWh, and rates) multiplies by the MVA base PSY5's value is on. Ohm, siemens and kV also need a voltage base, taken from the component's buses: an injector's bus, or a branch's arc, whose two ends share a base except across a transformer (whose impedances are per unit and never converted); where they differ, the from bus is used. LCC impedances are the exception: PSY5 put each on the voltage of the circuit it sits in, the DC line's r on scheduled_dc_voltage and each converter's on its own rectifier_base_voltage or inverter_base_voltage, and they are converted on that.\n\nA field whose PSY6 unit is physical and whose PSY5 storage is not known is never silently copied: it is listed under UNVERIFIED UNITS in the ConversionReport. An optional one is left unset with its PSY5 value kept in ext[\"psy5_unmapped\"]; a required one is written as PSY5 stored it. A new entry there means PSY5_STORAGE needs the field's convention.","title":"Converting each field into its declared unit"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Type-parameters-become-fields","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"PSY5 encodes variation in the type parameter; PSY6 in a property, often with a new vocabulary.\n\nPSY5 PSY6\nConstantReserve{ReserveUp} OnlineReserve, reserve_direction = \"UP\"\nVariableReserve{ReserveDown} OnlineReserve, reserve_direction = \"DOWN\"\n\nReserveUp → \"UP\" is a rename, not a passthrough. ConstantReserve and VariableReserve have identical PSY5 field sets — the distinction is carried by whether a requirement time series is attached, not by any field.\n\nReserve consolidation: spinning → OnlineReserve, non-spinning → OfflineReserve, ConstantReserveGroup → GroupReserve.","title":"Type parameters become fields"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Transformers-—-the-largest-restructuring","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"PSY6 has no Transformer2W, TapTransformer, PhaseShiftingTransformer or Transformer3W. Electrical data moves into a separate TransformerCircuit component, so one PSY5 component becomes several.\n\nPSY5 PSY6\nTransformer2W, TapTransformer, PhaseShiftingTransformer TwoWindingTransformer + 1 TransformerCircuit\nTransformer3W ThreeWindingTransformer + 3 TransformerCircuit\n\nConsequences worth knowing:\n\nWindingGroupNumber is gone; only the angle survives, as TransformerCircuit.alpha in radians. The enum is sparse and sign-inverted — GROUP_1 is −30°, not +30 — so it maps through a literal table, never n × 30°. UNDEFINED (a third of real transformers) means \"not specified\" and takes the schema default of 0.0.\nPhaseShiftingTransformer.α is already radians and copies verbatim. It never coexists with a winding group, so the two sources are never summed.\nThe 1-3 winding pair becomes 3-1: r_13/x_13/base_power_13 → r_31/x_31/base_power_31. The 1-2 and 2-3 pairs keep their names. A silent-corruption trap.\nAvailability and rating are circuit-level. Transformer3W's top-level available and rating have no PSY6 home; each circuit carries its own. A circuit is available only if both the transformer and its winding are (available && available_<winding>), so a transformer PSY5 marked out of service gets three unavailable circuits; the top-level value is kept in ext.\ng/b become one magnetizing_shunt (ComplexNumber). On a three-winding transformer it sits star-bus-to-ground, so shunt_location = \"STAR\" — unlike the two-winding case, whose primary_shunt genuinely is primary-side and takes the \"PRIMARY\" default.","title":"Transformers — the largest restructuring"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Discriminated-unions","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"PSY5 tags every nested object with __metadata__.type. PSY6 uses JSON-Schema oneOf with an explicit discriminator property that PSY5 has no field for. It must be synthesized, and it nests — a CostCurve contains a ValueCurve containing FunctionData, each needing its own.\n\nUnion Property Example\nProductionVariableCostCurve variable_cost_type CostCurve → COST\nValueCurve curve_type InputOutputCurve → INPUT_OUTPUT\nFunctionData function_type LinearFunctionData → LINEAR\nGenericOperationCost, HydroStorageGenerationCost cost_type ThermalGenerationCost → THERMAL\nTwoTerminalLoss curve_type \n\nOne branch carries no tag at all: ThermalGenerationCost's StartUpStages is identified by its {hot, warm, cold} key set.\n\nNarrowed unions differ from the general one. IncrementalCurve and AverageRateCurve accept only {LINEAR, PIECEWISE_STEP}, while InputOutputCurve accepts {LINEAR, PIECEWISE_LINEAR, QUADRATIC} — matching the Julia type bounds in InfrastructureSystems.","title":"Discriminated unions"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Time-series","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"The sidecar is rewritten, not copied. PSY5 keys one HDF5 group per time series UUID under /time_series and embeds its association table as a SQLite blob in a second dataset. PSY6 uses InfraStore, which addresses every array by its SHA-256 content hash and keeps the associations in a sibling catalog file:\n\n PSY5 PSY6 (InfraStore)\nArray identity the time series UUID the array's SHA-256 content hash\nArray location /time_series/<uuid>/data one packed HDF5 dataset per array group\nAssociations a SQLite blob inside the HDF5 time_series.h5.sqlite, beside the HDF5\nDuplicate data one group per series de-duplicated by content hash\n\nA byte copy would therefore produce a bundle whose arrays no reader can resolve: the UUID that keyed them no longer exists anywhere in the stack, and there is no catalog to say which association owns which array. So convert_time_series decodes each array and re-adds it through InfraStore.jl, which writes both halves. The .h5 and its .sqlite are one artifact and must travel together.\n\nPSY6's importer adopts that catalog as the System's own time series store rather than replaying the document's time_series_associations, so the catalog is the copy that is actually read. Both are written, and both carry the same declarations.\n\nThree element layouts and one time series type make the crossing:\n\nPSY5 PSY6\nCONSTANT scalars unchanged; InfraStore derives the dtype\nPiecewiseStepData, NaN-padded (n, 2) matrices one self-describing piecewise_step row\nSingleTimeSeries, Deterministic the same types, same array shapes\nDeterministicSingleTimeSeries derived by transform_single_time_series!\n\nA derived forecast stores no array of its own in PSY6 — it re-describes the SingleTimeSeries it came from. InfraStore derives from every series of one owner category (components, or supplemental attributes) at a resolution or from none. PSY5 and PSY6 both derive for components only, so a supplemental attribute's series, such as an outage probability, keeps no derived forecast. A sidecar whose derived rows cover only some of a category's series at a resolution aborts rather than gaining or losing forecasts. Every other layout and type (PiecewiseLinearData, Probabilistic, Scenarios) errors: the two stores agree on nothing but plain scalars, and a Probabilistic association row carries no percentiles to rebuild one from.\n\nThe association metadata moves too. PSY5 embeds a whole SQLite database inside the HDF5; PSY6 puts the rows in the document as time_series_associations, with time_series_storage_file naming the sidecar by basename. Four columns do not map straight across:\n\nPSY5 PSY6\nowner_uuid owner_id, an integer\ntime_series_uuid dropped with UUID identity\nmetadata_uuid dropped with UUID identity\nscaling_factor_multiplier unit_system + quantity_kind\n\nPSY5 stored a scaled series as a fraction and named an accessor to multiply it by on retrieval. PSY6 rescales nothing, so the multiplier's meaning is re-expressed: the values are per-unit on the owner's own base, which is unit_system = DEVICE_BASE, and the accessor's physical quantity becomes quantity_kind (a Core/units.json vocabulary name).\n\nThe reservoir accessors — get_storage_capacity, get_storage_target, get_inflow — get a basis but no quantity_kind: a reservoir level is an energy, a volume, or a head depending on the owner's level_data_type, which an association row does not carry. Those are counted in the conversion report as unmapped quantity_kind rather than guessed at.\n\nThe document's element_type and application_data are left unset. Both describe the stored array, and PSY6 reads an array's description from the catalog — where element_type is written — so filling them into the document too would add a second copy with no reader.","title":"Time series"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Document-structure","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":" PSY5 PSY6\nComponents one flat array, __metadata__-tagged map of type name → array\nSubcomponents data.masked_components (HybridSystem parts) ordinary components, referenced by id\nAttributes supplemental_attribute_manager supplemental_attributes + supplemental_attribute_associations\nVersion marker data_format_version: \"5.0.0\" none — only unit_system is self-describing","title":"Document structure"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#Fields-with-no-PSY6-home","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"Rule: data that would otherwise be lost is moved to ext. A PSY5 value with no PSY6 field is kept on the component it came from, in the document's ext table under the reserved key psy5_unmapped, and PSY6 merges it into that component's ext on import:\n\nget_ext(component)[\"psy5_unmapped\"]  # Dict(\"R_th\" => 5.0e-6, \"X_th\" => 5.0e-6, ...)\n\nKeys are the PSY5 field name, or Type.field for a field of a nested struct (e.g. ImportExportCost.ancillary_service_offers, head_to_volume_factor.input_at_zero).\nValues are exactly as PSY5 stored them, including its per-unit basis (device base for unit-bearing fields), so they are a record of the source, not PSY6 values.\nThe component's own PSY5 ext entries are carried alongside, unchanged. A PSY5 ext that already uses the key psy5_unmapped is an error rather than silently merged.\nEvery kept field is also listed under UNMAPPED FIELDS in the ConversionReport.\n\nExamples: Source.R_th/X_th; the HVDC lines' active_power_limits_from/_to (only from.max survives, as rating); a transformer control_objective written as UNDEFINED because no band data could be found for it.\n\nNon-physical values PSY6 rejects are treated the same way. A transformer winding base voltage (base_voltage_primary, _secondary, ...) or a VSC line's rated_dc_voltage of 0 or less, which PSY5 accepted (some MATPOWER cases and test systems record none), is left unset (the schema fields are optional). The value is kept in psy5_unmapped and counted under INVALID VALUES DROPPED in the ConversionReport. So is every value PSY5 stored relative to such a base (a VSC DC voltage setpoint or limit), since it has no physical value. A required field, including the VSC setpoint the converter's control mode selects, is written as PSY5 stored it, so the document stays valid. A bus's base_voltage is written as stored: PSY6's Line checks need one.\n\nWhere ext cannot hold it, the data is still lost, and only reported:\n\nSkipped components (a PSY5 type with no PSY6 counterpart, and the components that reference one) have no PSY6 component to carry an ext.\nDynamic models (DynamicGenerator, DynamicInverter, ...) have no home in the 0.2 schema and are skipped. A static device linked to one through dynamic_injector is kept without the link, rather than skipped with it, and is counted under DYNAMIC MODELS DROPPED in the ConversionReport.\nArc, TransmissionInterface and TransformerCircuit have no ext in PSY6. A two- or three-winding transformer's dropped fields go on the transformer, not its circuits.\n\nNot lost, but no longer a field of their own: services (now ServiceAssociation rows), WindingGroupNumber (now the circuit's alpha), Transformer3W.available/.rating (now per circuit), and TapTransformer.tap_limits/voltage_setpoint (now the circuit's tap_ratio_limits/controlled_voltage_limits when its control objective needs them).","title":"Fields with no PSY6 home"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/psy5_to_psy6_component_changes/#What-PSY6-cannot-yet-express","page":"PSY5 to PSY6 component changes","text":"Time-series-valued fields. PSY5 embeds a ForecastKey or StaticTimeSeriesKey directly in a value field — FuelCurve.fuel_cost and MarketBidCost.incremental_offer_curves in the corpus. PSY6 names such a series by the integer id of its time series association instead.\n\nFuelCurve.fuel_cost: converted. The key becomes fuel_cost_time_series, the association id of the series it names (same owner, name, kind, features and resolution). The ids are minted by the sidecar's catalog, which is written after the components, so the field is written as a placeholder during translation and filled in once the catalog exists (resolve_series_refs in src/convert.jl).\nMarketBidCost with time-series offer curves: not yet converted. PSY6's counterpart, MarketBidTimeSeriesCost, needs minimum_energy_offer, start_up, shut_down and both offer curves as time series, where PSY5 holds scalars (or nothing). Carrying it means creating series PSY5 never had; until that is decided, conversion throws.\n\nScalar operating costs, resolved. MarketBidCost.shut_down and no_load_cost are typed as a concrete InputOutputCurve; PSY5 writes a bare Float64. The schema now sanctions this: its description documents the \"legacy scalar promotion\" and its default gives the exact InputOutputCurve shape the converter builds (LinearFunctionData with constant_term = s, proportional_term = 0) — see Core/common.json. The converter promotes accordingly.","title":"What PSY6 cannot yet express"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/stub/","page":"Stub","text":"Please refer to the Reference section of the diataxis framework.","title":"Stub"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/generated_stub/","page":"stub","text":"Please refer to the Tutorial section of the diataxis framework. Unlike the other documentation sections, Tutorials are written as scripts, then automatically processed into markdown files and Jupyter notebooks using the Literate.jl package. This functionality is implemented in make_tutorials.jl.","title":"stub"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#The-units-transformation","page":"The units transformation","text":"","title":"The units transformation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#What-gets-transformed","page":"The units transformation","text":"A PSY6 SystemDocument carries no document-level unit system and no document-level base power. Every component blob is self-interpretable: it carries its own base_power, and any power-bearing field on it carries a required power_units declaration naming the basis that field's number is expressed in. A consumer holding one component in isolation — no document, no sibling components — can still read every value on it correctly.\n\nThis package writes that per-blob declaration. Converting a PSY5 System JSON bundle, it stamps power_units on every PSY6 model that declares the field.","title":"What gets transformed"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#Why-every-stamp-reads-COMPONENT_BASE","page":"The units transformation","text":"PSY5 already stores its numbers per-unit on a base — the component's own base_power when it declares one, the system base otherwise (base_power_for in src/base_power.jl supplies that fallback). The updater's job is to say what a number already is, not to change what it is. Every power_units this package writes is \"COMPONENT_BASE\", and no value is ever rescaled: a PSY5 0.8 reaches the PSY6 blob as 0.8. The stamp is a label, not a computation.","title":"Why every stamp reads COMPONENT_BASE"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#Vocabulary","page":"The units transformation","text":"PSY6's basis vocabulary has exactly two members: COMPONENT_BASE and NATURAL_UNITS. There is no DEVICE_BASE and no system-wide basis. A value historically expressed on a shared system base does not get a third label — it gets COMPONENT_BASE, with that shared base recorded as the blob's own base_power. \"Component\" and \"system\" are both just numbers in base_power; the only basis word left in the schema is COMPONENT_BASE.","title":"Vocabulary"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#Where-the-stamp-is-written","page":"The units transformation","text":"Two paths write power_units, both before any value in the model is touched:\n\nThe generic path (direct_translate in src/translate/dispatch.jl): for any PSY6 type that declares a power_units field, the translator adds power_units = \"COMPONENT_BASE\" to the constructor kwargs alongside base_power, whatever the PSY5 type being converted.\nThe transformer paths (src/translate/transformers.jl): TransformerCircuit is built by hand for both two-winding transformers (_build_circuit) and each winding of a three-winding transformer (_winding_circuit), so each stamps power_units = \"COMPONENT_BASE\" explicitly rather than through the generic dispatch.","title":"Where the stamp is written"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#The-cost-member-rename","page":"The units transformation","text":"PSY5 spells the variable cost field variable on ThermalGenerationCost, HydroGenerationCost, RenewableGenerationCost, and LoadCost; PSY6 requires variable_operation_cost. _rename_variable_operation_cost in src/translate/fields.jl renames the key before the recursive field copy (translate_value) walks the value, so the renamed payload lands in the required PSY6 member instead of being recorded as an unmapped PSY5 field with the required member left absent.","title":"The cost-member rename"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#What-else-governs-a-field's-units","page":"The units transformation","text":"Not every field reads power_units. A cost curve nested inside a component (a CostCurve or FuelCurve) carries its own power_units, resolved against the owning component's base_power — not a fresh basis of its own. Other quantities use other discriminators entirely: parameter_units, energy_units, and the rest of the UnitSystem family, each scoped to the field it annotates. A field with a fixed x-unit (for example frequency in Hz) needs no basis at all — it is already in its one physical unit. Which discriminator governs which field, and how to resolve a COMPONENT_BASE reading once you have found it, are schema questions; see Reference: the units page below.","title":"What else governs a field's units"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#Worked-example","page":"The units transformation","text":"Input, a PSY5 ThermalStandard (abbreviated — a real PSY5 blob carries more fields than shown here):\n\n{\n  \"__metadata__\": {\"type\": \"ThermalStandard\"},\n  \"internal\": {\"uuid\": {\"value\": \"uuid-gen1\"}},\n  \"name\": \"gen1\",\n  \"base_power\": 150.0,\n  \"active_power\": 0.8\n}\n\nOutput, the PSY6 blob translate_component produces for it (abbreviated the same way):\n\n{\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"name\": \"gen1\",\n  \"base_power\": 150.0,\n  \"power_units\": \"COMPONENT_BASE\",\n  \"active_power\": 0.8\n}\n\nactive_power is untouched — 0.8 in, 0.8 out — because it was already per-unit on base_power = 150.0; the only new thing is the power_units label declaring that basis. Verified by calling PowerSystemsUpdater.translate_component on this input directly against the code on this branch.","title":"Worked example"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/units_transformation/#Reference:-the-units-page","page":"The units transformation","text":"SiennaSchemas' units page is the authoritative reading guide: the decision procedure for resolving any field's unit from its discriminator and basis, and the full UnitSystem vocabulary this page only summarizes. (The site is pre-release and may 404 today; the URL is the permanent target, the same convention SiennaGridDB's README uses for its own units section.) Adding a new unit or annotation is a schema question, not a converter one — see docs/UNIT_ANNOTATIONS.md in the SiennaSchemas repository for the authoring rules.","title":"Reference: the units page"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/stub/","page":"stub","text":"Please refer to the How-to-Guides section of the diataxis framework.","title":"stub"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/stub/","page":"stub","text":"Please refer to the Explanation section of the diataxis framework.","title":"stub"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Public-API-Reference","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Public API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ConversionReport","page":"Public API","text":"Aggregated findings from one or more conversions. Root skips (unmapped_types) are counted apart from cascaded_skips, which are components dropped only because something they reference was dropped, so one missing type does not read as many failures.\n\nCounts are by type or (type, field):\n\nunmapped_fields: PSY5 fields with no PSY6 counterpart, kept in the component's ext.\nunverified_units: a PSY5 value that could not be converted to the physical unit PSY6 declares; written as stored if required, else kept in ext.\ndropped_dynamic_models: static devices kept without their dynamic model.\ndropped_invalid_values: non-physical PSY5 values (such as a base voltage of 0), left unset.\napproximate_mappings: written, but known not to reproduce PSY5 exactly.\nschema_defaults: schema defaults written where PowerSystems requires the field.\npsy5_defaults: PSY5's own defaults filled for fields an older file omits.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ConversionReport"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemsUpdater.ConversionResult","page":"Public API","text":"The result of one conversion: the PCOM.SystemDocument, the ConversionReport, and the time series .h5 sidecar path (nothing without time series); its .sqlite catalog sits beside it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.ConversionResult"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#PowerSystemsUpdater.convert_system-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Public API","text":"convert_system(\n    src::AbstractString,\n    out_dir::AbstractString;\n    report,\n    force\n) -> ConversionResult\n\n\nConvert one PSY5 case into out_dir/system.json plus, with time series, the InfraStore pair out_dir/time_series.h5 and out_dir/time_series.h5.sqlite. The catalog also holds the supplemental attribute associations, so PSY6 can adopt it read-only.\n\nThe document's time series association rows are read back from the sidecar (convert_time_series), since only its catalog has the uri/data_hash/etc. PSY6 validates. Passing the same report to repeated calls accumulates findings across systems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.convert_system"},{"category":"section","location":"#PowerSystemsUpdater.jl","page":"Welcome Page","text":"","title":"PowerSystemsUpdater.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Overview","page":"Welcome Page","text":"PowerSystemsUpdater.jl is a Julia package that provides tools for updating and managing power systems data.","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"#About-Sienna","page":"Welcome Page","text":"PowerSystemsUpdater is part of the National Laboratory of the Rockies (formerly known as NREL)'s Sienna ecosystem, an open source framework for scheduling problems and dynamic simulations for power systems. The Sienna ecosystem can be found on github. It contains three applications:\n\nSienna\\Data enables efficient data input, analysis, and transformation\nSienna\\Ops enables enables system scheduling simulations by formulating and solving optimization problems\nSienna\\Dyn enables system transient analysis including small signal stability and full system dynamic simulations\n\nEach application uses multiple packages in the Julia programming language.","title":"About Sienna"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation-and-Quick-Links","page":"Welcome Page","text":"Sienna installation page: Instructions to install PowerSystemsUpdater.jl and other Sienna packages\nSienna Documentation Hub: Links to other Sienna packages' documentation","title":"Installation and Quick Links"}]
}
